-- Publish source-aligned Traditional Chinese translation for DSE 2024 Part A.
insert into public.dse_reading_translations (article_id, locale, source_sha256, content, published)
values ('dse-2024-a', 'zh-Hant', '8d30704e978bf29a18e9af7a74e9ae6f716a573359a49cfaf5b51387a2e65d27', '{"schemaVersion":1,"articleId":"dse-2024-a","locale":"zh-Hant","entries":[{"path":"title","source":"Hong Kong’s Banyan Trees","translation":"香港的榕樹"},{"path":"sourceLabel","source":"HKDSE 2024 English Language Paper 1 Part A","translation":"2024 年香港中學文憑考試英國語文科卷一 A 部分"},{"path":"sourceHeading","source":"Government defends axing century-old banyans on safety grounds & A Tree Worthy of Worship: Hong Kong’s Banyans","translation":"政府以安全理由為砍伐百年榕樹辯護；值得敬拜的樹：香港的榕樹"},{"path":"paragraphs/0/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 1","translation":"文章1，第 1 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/0/text","source":"Four trees collapsed in Hong Kong on Monday morning following a night of heavy rain. This comes after the government’s controversial decision to cut down four century-old Chinese banyans after several similar trees fell from stone walls during recent storms.","translation":"一夜大雨後，星期一早上香港有四棵樹倒塌。此前數場暴風雨使幾棵同類樹木從石牆上倒下，政府隨後作出備受爭議的決定，砍去四棵百年中國榕樹。"},{"path":"paragraphs/1/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 2","translation":"文章1，第 2 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/1/text","source":"The report of the fallen trees comes days after experts expressed anger over the Highways Department’s controversial felling of four century-old banyan trees in Sai Ying Pun, without consulting a panel advising the government on tree management.","translation":"樹木倒塌的消息傳出數天前，路政署未有諮詢向政府提供樹木管理意見的小組，就在西營盤砍伐四棵百年榕樹；專家對此表示憤怒。"},{"path":"paragraphs/2/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 3","translation":"文章1，第 3 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/2/text","source":"The government cited ‘unforeseen’ circumstances and considerations of public safety, after a giant banyan tree growing out of a masonry wall in Sai Ying Pun collapsed on 22 July. A neighbouring tree was cut down immediately as cracks were found in the wall behind it.","translation":"7 月 22 日，西營盤一棵長在石砌牆上的巨型榕樹倒塌後，政府以「未能預見」的情況及公眾安全考慮作解釋。當時發現鄰近一棵樹後方的牆壁有裂縫，那棵樹隨即被砍掉。"},{"path":"paragraphs/3/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 4","translation":"文章1，第 4 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/3/text","source":"The Head of the Developments Bureau’s Tree Management Office said the trees in Sai Ying Pun were rooted in old stone masonry walls on a slope of almost 80 degrees.","translation":"發展局樹木管理辦事處主管表示，西營盤的樹紮根於舊石砌牆中，而牆所在的斜坡坡度接近八十度。"},{"path":"paragraphs/4/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 5","translation":"文章1，第 5 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/4/text","source":"Following the collapse on 22 July, the Highways Department’s contractor inspected the remaining trees and carried out major trimming work. But by midweek last week, cracks were found in the wall behind the trees and were seen to have worsened.","translation":"7 月 22 日的倒塌事故後，路政署承辦商檢查餘下的樹，並作大幅修剪。但到了上星期中，樹後方的牆出現裂縫，而且裂縫已經惡化。"},{"path":"paragraphs/5/label","source":"Text 1 - Paragraph 6","translation":"文章1，第 6 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/5/text","source":"“Since the trees were growing on this wall, we could not evaluate the trees and the wall separately,” said the Head of the Tree Management Office. “We agree with the department that the trees had to be removed immediately. They could have collapsed and pulled the wall with them.”","translation":"樹木管理辦事處主管說：「由於樹長在這面牆上，我們不能把樹和牆分開評估。我們同意路政署必須立即移走那些樹。它們可能倒塌，連牆也一起拉倒。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/6/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 1","translation":"文章2，第 1 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/6/text","source":"Mr Lam was a teenager when he installed a shrine to the local earth god under a banyan tree in Tai Hang. “That was over 70 years ago,” he says. After World War II, he received permission from the government to transform the shrine into a temple.","translation":"林先生還是少年時，就在大坑一棵榕樹下為本地土地神設置神龕。「那是七十多年前的事了，」他說。第二次世界大戰後，他取得政府許可，把神龕改建為廟宇。"},{"path":"paragraphs/7/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 2","translation":"文章2，第 2 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/7/text","source":"It is no coincidence that Lam’s temple started with a banyan tree. These behemoths are ubiquitous in Hong Kong, growing in parks, street planters and even between the cracks of stone walls. Their imposing presence defines the cityscape. “If Hong Kong was abandoned it would be taken over by banyans in a few hundred years,” says Jim Chi-yung, chair of the University of Hong Kong’s Department of Geography, who is popularly known as the Tree Professor for his arboreal enthusiasm.","translation":"林先生的廟宇從榕樹開始，絕非巧合。這些巨樹在香港隨處可見，生長在公園、街道花槽，甚至石牆裂縫之間。它們雄偉的姿態塑造了城市景觀。香港大學地理系主任、因熱愛樹木而被稱為「樹木教授」的詹志勇說：「如果香港被遺棄，幾百年後榕樹便會接管整座城市。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/8/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 3","translation":"文章2，第 3 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/8/text","source":"Banyan trees are immediately recognisable for their spindly aerial roots, which cast outwards in search of water and nutrition. When a root finds a suitable source, either in the soil or another tree, it becomes a thick, woody trunk. This is what allows the banyan to grow in varied conditions, which is why they are the most prominent forms of greenery in the hilliest and most densely packed parts of Hong Kong. Jim has counted more than 1,100 trees growing from the sheer surfaces of masonry walls on Hong Kong Island. “They can become 20 metres tall, as big as trees growing out of the ground, except they are growing out from the wall,” he says.","translation":"榕樹纖細的氣根向外伸展，尋找水分和養分，因此很容易辨認。當根在泥土或另一棵樹中找到適合的來源，就會長成粗壯的木質樹幹。這使榕樹能在各種環境生長，也令它成為香港山多、建築密集地區最顯眼的綠化植物。詹志勇數過香港島石砌牆陡直表面長出的榕樹，超過一千一百棵。他說：「它們可長到二十米高，跟地上長出的樹一樣大，只是它們從牆上長出來。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/9/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 4","translation":"文章2，第 4 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/9/text","source":"When I first met Jim, in 2009, he took me to Forbes Street in Kennedy Town, where 22 banyans grow out of the surface of a 12-metre-high stone wall, which was built using a traditional Hakka technique that does not require mortar between stone joints. Seeds carried by the wind or dropped by birds find their way into the cracks. As the tree grows, its roots plunge dozens of metres into the soil behind the wall.","translation":"我在 2009 年初次認識詹志勇時，他帶我到堅尼地城科士街。那裏有二十二棵榕樹從一面十二米高的石牆長出來。石牆採用傳統客家工法建造，石塊接縫之間毋須灰漿。種子被風吹來，或由鳥兒投下，落進裂縫。樹木生長時，根便向牆後泥土深入數十米。"},{"path":"paragraphs/10/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 5","translation":"文章2，第 5 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/10/text","source":"Jim loves the way the banyans form a lush green canopy across Forbes Street. He sits on a number of government committees, and he told me he once proposed pedestrianising the street to make it a destination for al fresco dining, a place where people could sit and relax under the shade of the banyans. The government’s reception was frosty.","translation":"詹志勇喜歡榕樹在科士街上方形成茂密的綠色樹冠。他擔任多個政府委員會成員，曾向我說，他提議把街道改成行人專用區，成為露天用餐的目的地，讓人們可以在榕樹樹蔭下坐着休息。政府的反應卻很冷淡。"},{"path":"paragraphs/11/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 6","translation":"文章2，第 6 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/11/text","source":"“See what’s happening here?” he asks, touching a root that had been concreted over to stop it from growing. “The people who do this, they don’t understand trees. They’re defacing heritage. Imagine doing this to an ancient monument.”","translation":"「看到這裏發生甚麼事嗎？」他觸摸一條被水泥封住、因而無法生長的樹根，這樣問道。「做這種事的人不懂樹。他們在破壞文物。試想像有人這樣對待一座古蹟。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/12/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 7","translation":"文章2，第 7 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/12/text","source":"Last summer, after days of heavy rain, a wall tree collapsed onto Bonham Road, which led the Highways Department to surreptitiously chop down four healthy banyans nearby. Their sudden removal was defended by the government as a precautionary measure, but experts like Jim said it was an unnecessary overreaction. It sparked outrage from local residents, who tied balloons and messages of support to the trees’ roots, which still clung to the wall that had supported them for 100 years.","translation":"去年夏天，連日大雨後一棵牆樹倒在般咸道上，路政署於是暗中砍掉附近四棵健康的榕樹。政府辯稱突然砍樹是預防措施，但詹志勇等專家認為這是沒有必要的過度反應。事件引起居民憤怒；他們把氣球和支持訊息繫在仍攀附着那面百年石牆的樹根上。"},{"path":"paragraphs/13/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 8","translation":"文章2，第 8 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/13/text","source":"Respect for banyans runs deep in southern Chinese culture. Banyan trees are considered to have excellent feng shui, symbolising longevity, fecundity and perseverance. They are also believed to be home to earth gods, the indigenous deities that protect each village, and shrines are often built at their base. In many cases, people worship the trees themselves, not just the earth gods. That is the case in Lam Tsuen, where a pair of banyans known as the Wishing Trees have become a tourist attraction. Visitors write their wish on a piece of yellow paper, tie it to an orange and toss it onto one of the trees’ branches. After the weight of all the wishes caused a branch to collapse in 2005, worshippers were instructed to tie their wishes to a plastic tree instead.","translation":"華南文化對榕樹的尊崇根深蒂固。人們認為榕樹風水極佳，象徵長壽、繁衍和堅毅；也相信榕樹是保護各村莊的土地神的居所，所以常在樹腳建神龕。許多時候，人們敬拜的不只是土地神，也包括榕樹本身。林村的一對「許願樹」便是例子，它們已成為旅遊景點。遊客把願望寫在黃紙上，繫在橙子上，再拋到樹枝上。2005 年，願望的重量令一條樹枝倒塌，於是拜祭者被要求改把願望繫在塑膠樹上。"},{"path":"paragraphs/14/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 9","translation":"文章2，第 9 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/14/text","source":"Anthropologist P.Y.L. Ng notes that banyan trees were worshipped because they were often the only surviving trees in a landscape that had been steadily deforested over hundreds of years. “Its wood is gnarled and so cannot be used as timber. It will not flame and so cannot be used for firewood. Its very lack of useful properties ensures its invincibility and survival,” he wrote in a 1983 study of the New Territories.","translation":"人類學家吳丕龍指出，人們敬拜榕樹，是因為在數百年來持續砍伐森林的地方，榕樹往往是僅存的樹木。他在 1983 年一項新界研究中寫道：「榕木盤曲，不能用作木材；它不易燃燒，也不能用作柴薪。正因缺乏實用特性，它才得以不被摧毀並存活下來。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/15/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 10","translation":"文章2，第 10 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/15/text","source":"The 17th century playwright Li Yu saw the banyan tree as a symbol of love. “Anytime a smaller tree grows before a banyan tree, this banyan will sooner or later lean its body towards the smaller tree. After a time, it wraps its branches around the smaller tree’s body, and the smaller tree gradually falls into the banyan’s embrace. The two trees become one, so that even if you cut them with an axe you would not be able to separate them.”","translation":"十七世紀劇作家李漁把榕樹視為愛情的象徵。「每當一棵小樹長在榕樹前，榕樹遲早會朝小樹傾斜。過了一段時間，它用枝條環繞小樹的身體，小樹漸漸投入榕樹的懷抱。兩棵樹合而為一，即使用斧頭砍，也無法把它們分開。」"},{"path":"paragraphs/16/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 11","translation":"文章2，第 11 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/16/text","source":"Modern Hong Kong has found ways to accommodate banyan trees. To Yuen Street near City University forks around a particularly large banyan, an accommodation also made on Dragon Road near Victoria Park. Nearly two-thirds of the 481 trees on the government’s Register of Old and Valuable Trees are banyans. According to the government, there are 29,000 banyans under maintenance in city parks and streets, though many more exist undocumented in the wild. A total of 3,491 new banyans have been planted in the city since 2011.","translation":"現代香港找到與榕樹共存的方法。城市大學附近的桃源街在一棵特別巨大的榕樹前分岔，維多利亞公園附近的龍道也作了類似安排。政府《古樹名木冊》所列的四百八十一棵樹中，近三分之二是榕樹。政府表示，市內公園及街道有二萬九千棵榕樹受到保養，郊野中還有更多未記錄在案的榕樹。自 2011 年起，市內共種了三千四百九十一棵新榕樹。"},{"path":"paragraphs/17/label","source":"Text 2 - Paragraph 12","translation":"文章2，第 12 段"},{"path":"paragraphs/17/text","source":"And while the future of many old and prominent banyans is contentious you can count on banyans to find a way to survive even in the most difficult conditions. New sprouts are already growing from the stumps of the severed banyan trees on Bonham Road. There is a reason they are worshipped, after all.","translation":"雖然不少古老而顯眼的榕樹前途仍有爭議，但你可以相信榕樹即使在最艱難的環境下，也會找到生存之道。般咸道被砍榕樹的樹樁上，已長出新芽。人們敬拜榕樹，畢竟是有原因的。"},{"path":"instructions/paper","source":"Read Texts 1 and 2 and answer questions 1–23. (42 marks)","translation":"閱讀文章一及文章二，回答第 1 至 23 題。（42 分）"},{"path":"questions/0/prompt","source":"Based on the information in paragraph 1, complete the sentence by selecting the best option from the choices below. (2 marks)","translation":"根據第 1 段資料，從選項選出最佳答案完成句子。（2 分）"},{"path":"questions/0/context","source":"(i) ______ banyan trees were removed while several others (ii) ______ as a result of heavy rainfall.","translation":"(i) ______ 棵榕樹被移走，而另外幾棵則因大雨 (ii) ______。"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/0/options/0","source":"A. Eight","translation":"A. 八棵"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/0/options/1","source":"B. One hundred","translation":"B. 一百棵"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/0/options/2","source":"C. Four-year-old","translation":"C. 四年樹齡的"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/0/options/3","source":"D. Four hundred-year-old","translation":"D. 四棵百年樹齡的"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/1/options/0","source":"A. loosened","translation":"A. 鬆脫"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/1/options/1","source":"B. fell down","translation":"B. 倒下"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/1/options/2","source":"C. were crushed","translation":"C. 被壓碎"},{"path":"questions/0/parts/1/options/3","source":"D. were cut down","translation":"D. 被砍倒"},{"path":"questions/1/prompt","source":"According to paragraphs 1 and 2, why was the ‘decision’ (line 2) considered ‘controversial’ (line 2)?","translation":"根據第 1 及第 2 段，為甚麼這個「決定」（第 2 行）被視為「有爭議」（第 2 行）？"},{"path":"questions/2/prompt","source":"According to paragraph 5, how did the wall become a problem?","translation":"根據第 5 段，牆壁如何變成問題？"},{"path":"questions/3/prompt","source":"Who or what does ‘them’ (line 17) refer to?","translation":"「它們」（第 17 行）指誰或甚麼？"},{"path":"questions/4/prompt","source":"According to Text 1, are the following statements True (T), False (F) or Not Given (NG)? (3 marks)","translation":"根據文章一，判斷以下陳述是正確（T）、錯誤（F）還是未有提及（NG）。（3 分）"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/0/label","source":"(i) Two government departments had the same view towards the tree felling decision.","translation":"(i) 兩個政府部門對砍樹決定有相同看法。"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/0/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/0/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/0/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/1/label","source":"(ii) The trees in Sai Ying Pun were taken down after experts were upset.","translation":"(ii) 西營盤的樹在專家感到憤怒後才被砍下。"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/1/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/1/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/1/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/2/label","source":"(iii) No one was hurt by the fallen trees.","translation":"(iii) 沒有人因倒塌的樹木受傷。"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/2/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/2/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/4/parts/2/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/5/prompt","source":"What is the text type of Text 1?","translation":"文章一屬於甚麼文體？"},{"path":"questions/5/options/0","source":"A. A news report","translation":"A. 新聞報道"},{"path":"questions/5/options/1","source":"B. Health and safety advice","translation":"B. 健康與安全建議"},{"path":"questions/5/options/2","source":"C. A profile of banyan trees in Hong Kong","translation":"C. 香港榕樹介紹文章"},{"path":"questions/5/options/3","source":"D. A leaflet promoting Hong Kong’s heritage","translation":"D. 宣傳香港文化遺產的小冊子"},{"path":"questions/6/prompt","source":"With reference to paragraph 1, complete the sentence below.","translation":"根據第 1 段，完成以下句子。"},{"path":"questions/6/context","source":"Over 70 years ago, Lam installed a shrine, which has been ______________________________.","translation":"七十多年前，林先生設置了一個神龕，後來它被 ______________________________。"},{"path":"questions/7/prompt","source":"What does the phrase ‘these behemoths’ (line 4) refer to?","translation":"「這些巨樹」（第 4 行）指甚麼？"},{"path":"questions/8/prompt","source":"What does Jim imply when he says ‘If Hong Kong was abandoned it would be taken over by banyans in a few hundred years’ (line 6)?","translation":"詹志勇說「如果香港被遺棄，幾百年後榕樹便會接管整座城市」（第 6 行），他暗示甚麼？"},{"path":"questions/9/prompt","source":"Find a word in paragraph 2 which can be replaced by each word or phrase given below. (2 marks)","translation":"在第 2 段找出可替代以下詞句的字。（2 分）"},{"path":"questions/9/parts/0/label","source":"(i) ‘seen everywhere’","translation":"(i) 「到處可見」"},{"path":"questions/9/parts/1/label","source":"(ii) ‘significant’","translation":"(ii) 「重要／顯著」"},{"path":"questions/10/prompt","source":"Below is a summary of paragraph 3. In five of the lines there is ONE mistake. If you find a mistake, underline it and replace the word with one that expresses the correct idea. Write the word in the Correction column. Both grammar and spelling must be correct. In one of the lines, there is no mistake; put a tick (✓) in the Correction column. One has been done for you as an example. (5 marks)","translation":"以下是第 3 段的摘要。其中五行各有一個錯誤；找出錯誤後，在更正欄填入表達正確意思的字。文法和拼寫都必須正確。另有一行沒有錯誤，請在更正欄打勾（✓）。已提供一個例子。（5 分）"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/0/0/text","source":"Summary","translation":"摘要"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/0/1/text","source":"Correction","translation":"更正"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/1/0/text","source":"(i) Thin airborne branches seek food, making banyan trees easily identifiable.","translation":"(i) 纖細的空中枝條尋找食物，使榕樹容易辨認。"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/2/0/text","source":"(ii) Over 1,100 banyans growing out of stone walls on Hong Kong Island","translation":"(ii) 香港島有超過一千一百棵從石牆上長出的榕樹"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/3/0/text","source":"(iii) were recorded by Jim Chi-yung. Finding protection from another","translation":"(iii) 由詹志勇記錄。從另一棵樹或泥土中找到保護後"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/4/0/text","source":"(iv) tree or the soil enables it to produce a thin trunk. Since banyans","translation":"(iv) 榕樹便能長出纖細的樹幹。由於榕樹"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/5/0/text","source":"(v) grow in few situations they are the most dominant form of greenery","translation":"(v) 只在少數環境生長，所以它們是最顯眼的綠化植物"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/6/0/text","source":"even in areas that have very little space or are very flat (example)","translation":"即使在空間狹小或地勢十分平坦的地方（例子）"},{"path":"questions/10/tables/0/rows/6/1/text","source":"hilly","translation":"多山"},{"path":"questions/10/parts/0/label","source":"(i) correction","translation":"(i) 更正"},{"path":"questions/10/parts/1/label","source":"(ii) correction","translation":"(ii) 更正"},{"path":"questions/10/parts/2/label","source":"(iii) correction","translation":"(iii) 更正"},{"path":"questions/10/parts/3/label","source":"(iv) correction","translation":"(iv) 更正"},{"path":"questions/10/parts/4/label","source":"(v) correction","translation":"(v) 更正"},{"path":"questions/11/prompt","source":"Complete the notes about paragraph 4 by writing ONE word taken from the paragraph in each blank below. (4 marks)","translation":"根據第 4 段的內容，在每個空格填入取自該段的一個字，完成筆記。（4 分）"},{"path":"questions/11/context","source":"Jim shows the writer trees growing out of a stone wall built according to a (i) ______ method. This type of wall needs no (ii) ______ in the gaps between each stone. He explains that birds let go of banyan (iii) ______ or they are carried by the wind and fall into these gaps. It is here that very long roots (iv) ______.","translation":"詹志勇帶作者看一面按 (i) ______ 方法建造的石牆上長出的樹。這種牆的石塊之間不需要 (ii) ______。他解釋，鳥兒把榕樹的 (iii) ______ 放下，或風吹着它們落入石縫。很長的樹根便在這裏 (iv) ______。"},{"path":"questions/12/prompt","source":"Complete the summary of paragraph 5 by selecting the best option from the choices below. (3 marks)","translation":"從選項選出最佳答案，完成第 5 段的摘要。（3 分）"},{"path":"questions/12/context","source":"Jim is impressed by the way that the trees create a green (i) ______ that covers the road. He says that he once suggested creating a (ii) ______ street with restaurants for people to eat outside under the banyans. The government reacted in (iii) ______ way to the idea.","translation":"詹志勇欣賞這些樹形成覆蓋道路的綠色 (i) ______。他曾建議把街道改為 (ii) ______ 街道，讓人在榕樹下的餐廳露天用餐。政府對這個想法作出 (iii) ______ 反應。"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/0/options/0","source":"A. banyan","translation":"A. 榕樹"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/0/options/1","source":"B. umbrella","translation":"B. 傘"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/0/options/2","source":"C. backdrop","translation":"C. 背景"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/0/options/3","source":"D. destination","translation":"D. 目的地"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/1/options/0","source":"A. traffic-free","translation":"A. 無車輛通行的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/1/options/1","source":"B. driver-friendly","translation":"B. 方便駕駛者的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/1/options/2","source":"C. pedestrian-free","translation":"C. 沒有行人的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/1/options/3","source":"D. environmentally-friendly","translation":"D. 環保的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/2/options/0","source":"A. a warm","translation":"A. 熱情的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/2/options/1","source":"B. a negative","translation":"B. 負面的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/2/options/2","source":"C. a sarcastic","translation":"C. 諷刺的"},{"path":"questions/12/parts/2/options/3","source":"D. an optimistic","translation":"D. 樂觀的"},{"path":"questions/13/prompt","source":"What does ‘it’ (line 22) refer to?","translation":"「它」（第 22 行）指甚麼？"},{"path":"questions/14/prompt","source":"In paragraph 6, what is Jim’s attitude towards people who concrete over roots: Positive, negative or neutral? Give one reason from Text 2 to support your answer.","translation":"在第 6 段，詹志勇對把樹根封在水泥下的人持正面、負面還是中立態度？請從文章二舉出一個理由支持你的答案。"},{"path":"questions/15/prompt","source":"What does ‘an unnecessary overreaction’ (line 27) refer to?","translation":"「沒有必要的過度反應」（第 27 行）指甚麼？"},{"path":"questions/16/prompt","source":"According to paragraph 7, why did local residents in Bonham Road attach balloons to the tree roots?","translation":"根據第 7 段，般咸道居民為甚麼把氣球繫在樹根上？"},{"path":"questions/17/prompt","source":"According to paragraph 8, are the following statements True (T), False (F) or Not Given (NG)? (3 marks)","translation":"根據第 8 段，判斷以下陳述是正確（T）、錯誤（F）還是未有提及（NG）。（3 分）"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/0/label","source":"(i) Visitors to Lam Tsuen buy prepared wishes to put on the tree.","translation":"(i) 林村遊客購買預先寫好的願望，掛到樹上。"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/0/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/0/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/0/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/1/label","source":"(ii) Since 2005 there has been a decline in the number of worshippers at Lam Tsuen.","translation":"(ii) 自 2005 年起，林村拜祭者的人數減少。"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/1/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/1/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/1/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/2/label","source":"(iii) Shrines are frequently built in the branches of trees.","translation":"(iii) 神龕經常建在樹枝上。"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/2/options/0","source":"TRUE","translation":"正確"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/2/options/1","source":"FALSE","translation":"錯誤"},{"path":"questions/17/parts/2/options/2","source":"NOT GIVEN","translation":"未提及"},{"path":"questions/18/prompt","source":"Why did the ‘lack of useful properties’ (line 39) ensure the survival of banyans?","translation":"為甚麼「缺乏實用特性」（第 39 行）反而確保榕樹存活？"},{"path":"questions/19/prompt","source":"Provide ONE example of how the behaviour of banyans can be seen as ‘a symbol of love’ (line 41).","translation":"舉出一個例子，說明榕樹的行為如何被視為「愛的象徵」（第 41 行）。"},{"path":"questions/20/prompt","source":"According to paragraph 11, give ONE example of how the government is protecting banyan trees.","translation":"根據第 11 段，舉出政府保護榕樹的一個例子。"},{"path":"questions/21/prompt","source":"According to Text 2, what quality of banyan trees does the writer have in mind when he says ‘There is a reason they are worshipped, after all’ (line 52)?","translation":"根據文章二，作者說「人們敬拜榕樹，畢竟是有原因的」（第 52 行）時，心目中想到榕樹甚麼特質？"},{"path":"questions/22/prompt","source":"Use the information in Text 2 to match each of the following comments with a person/organisation mentioned in the text. Write the letter of the comment in the Answer column. One comment is NOT used. One has been done for you as an example. Use each letter ONCE only. (5 marks)","translation":"根據文章二，把每句評論配對到文中提及的人物或機構。把評論的字母填在答案欄。其中一個評論不會使用。已提供一個例子。每個字母只能使用一次。（5 分）"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/0","source":"A. Banyan trees represent love.","translation":"A. 榕樹象徵愛情。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/1","source":"B. There are too many trees growing out of walls.","translation":"B. 從牆上長出的樹實在太多。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/2","source":"C. We needed to play it safe. We just had to be cautious.","translation":"C. 我們需要以安全為先，必須謹慎。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/3","source":"D. This tree has been part of my life for so long now.","translation":"D. 這棵樹陪伴我人生已很久。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/4","source":"E. I don’t mind if it’s artificial as long as my wishes are heard.","translation":"E. 只要我的願望能被聽見，就算它是人工的，我也不介意。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/5","source":"F. It’s useless. The wood is not smooth enough to make anything out of.","translation":"F. 它沒有實用價值。木材不夠平滑，不能用來製作東西。"},{"path":"questions/22/optionBank/6","source":"G. My nickname is accurate. I can tell you everything there is to know about banyans.","translation":"G. 我的綽號名副其實。我可以告訴你所有關於榕樹的事。"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/0/0/text","source":"Person/organisation","translation":"人物／機構"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/0/1/text","source":"Answer","translation":"答案"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/1/0/text","source":"Li Yu","translation":"李漁"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/1/1/text","source":"A (example)","translation":"A（例子）"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/2/0/text","source":"Mr Lam","translation":"林先生"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/3/0/text","source":"P. Y. L. Ng","translation":"吳丕龍"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/4/0/text","source":"Jim Chi-yung","translation":"詹志勇"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/5/0/text","source":"Visitor to Lam Tsuen","translation":"林村遊客"},{"path":"questions/22/tables/0/rows/6/0/text","source":"The Highways Department","translation":"路政署"},{"path":"questions/22/parts/0/label","source":"(i) Mr Lam","translation":"(i) 林先生"},{"path":"questions/22/parts/1/label","source":"(ii) P. Y. L. Ng","translation":"(ii) 吳丕龍"},{"path":"questions/22/parts/2/label","source":"(iii) Jim Chi-yung","translation":"(iii) 詹志勇"},{"path":"questions/22/parts/3/label","source":"(iv) Visitor to Lam Tsuen","translation":"(iv) 林村遊客"},{"path":"questions/22/parts/4/label","source":"(v) The Highways Department","translation":"(v) 路政署"}]}'::jsonb, true)
